        "original_id": "04ed5e32-f96a-50eb-a41c-8fd1c29bf006",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ransom Riggs, John Berry, Joan Fontaine, Mark Stevens\n- Works: Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children, Hollow City, From This Day Forward\n- Roles: writer, filmmaker, film director\n- Topics: Hollywood blacklist, self-exile in France\n\nFacts:\n- John Berry was born on September 6, 1917, and he was an American film director.\n- From This Day Forward is a 1946 American drama film directed by John Berry and starring Joan Fontaine and Mark Stevens.\n- Ransom Riggs was born on February 3, 1979, and he is an American writer and filmmaker.\n- Ransom Riggs is best known for the book Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children.\n- John Berry went into self-exile in France when the Hollywood blacklist interrupted his career.\n- Hollow City is a 2014 dark fantasy novel by Ransom Riggs.\n- Hollow City is a sequel to Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar Children.\n- John Berry died on November 29, 1999.",
